---
const SITE = 'https://data.worldbatteryhub.com';
const groups = [
  { g: 'H4 (L1)', dim: '~207 × 175 × 190 mm', terminal: 'SAE / DIN post' },
  { g: 'H5 (L2)', dim: '~242 × 175 × 190 mm', terminal: 'SAE / DIN post' },
  { g: 'H6 (L3)', dim: '~278 × 175 × 190 mm', terminal: 'SAE / DIN post' },
  { g: 'H7 (L4)', dim: '~315 × 175 × 190 mm', terminal: 'SAE / DIN post' },
  { g: 'H8 (L5)', dim: '~352 × 175 × 190 mm', terminal: 'SAE / DIN post' },
  { g: 'H9 (L6)', dim: '~394 × 175 × 190 mm', terminal: 'SAE / DIN post' },
  { g: 'JIS D23 (55/65/75D23)', dim: '~232 × 173 × 202–225 mm', terminal: 'JIS type A (small/large post)' },
  { g: 'JIS N150 (145G51)', dim: '~508 × 222 × 212 mm', terminal: 'JIS type A (large taper post)' },
  { g: 'JIS N200 (190H52)', dim: '~520 × 278 × 220 mm', terminal: 'JIS type A (large taper post)' },
  { g: 'BCI Group 31', dim: '~330 × 173 × 240 mm', terminal: 'SAE stud / post' },
  { g: 'BCI Group 8D', dim: '~527 × 283 × 250 mm', terminal: 'SAE stud' },
];
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Battery Dimensions &amp; Terminals | World Battery Hub</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Physical fitment reference — typical length, width, height and terminal type by battery group (H4-H9, JIS, BCI). Dimensions are typical and must be confirmed against the original battery." />
    <link rel="canonical" href={`${SITE}/dimensions-terminals/`} />
    <style>
      body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 0; color: #1e293b; line-height: 1.6; }
      .container { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }
      h1, h2 { color: #0f1f3d; }
      a { color: #1d4ed8; }
      .muted { color: #64748b; font-size: 0.85rem; }
      .box { background: #eff6ff; border-left: 4px solid #1d4ed8; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 14px 0; }
      table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.95rem; }
      th, td { text-align: left; padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e9f0; }
      th { color: #0f1f3d; }
    </style>
  
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={"{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"@id\": \"https://data.worldbatteryhub.com/dimensions-terminals/\", \"url\": \"https://data.worldbatteryhub.com/dimensions-terminals/\", \"name\": \"Dimensions Terminals\", \"publisher\": {\"@id\": \"https://worldbatteryhub.com/#organization\"}, \"isPartOf\": {\"@id\": \"https://data.worldbatteryhub.com/\"}}"} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={"{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Battery Data\", \"item\": \"https://data.worldbatteryhub.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Dimensions Terminals\", \"item\": \"https://data.worldbatteryhub.com/dimensions-terminals/\"}]}"} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Battery Dimensions &amp; Terminals</h1>
      <p class="muted">Battery Data · Last reviewed 2026-09-15</p>

      <div class="box">
        <strong>Direct answer:</strong> A battery group fixes the <strong>physical footprint</strong> — length, width,
        height — and the <strong>terminal type and position</strong>. Dimensions vary slightly by manufacturer and terminal
        style, so the values below are <strong>typical</strong> and must be confirmed against the original battery before
        replacement.
      </div>

      <h2>Typical dimensions and terminals by group</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Typical L × W × H</th><th>Terminal</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {groups.map((x) => (
            <tr><td><strong>{x.g}</strong></td><td>{x.dim}</td><td>{x.terminal}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Terminal types</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>SAE post</strong> — the tapered round posts standard on most North American and European batteries (positive larger than negative).</li>
        <li><strong>JIS type A / B</strong> — the Japanese tapered posts; the "A" post is larger and carries more current (heavy-duty).</li>
        <li><strong>Stud (threaded)</strong> — a threaded terminal common on commercial and marine batteries.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>The terminal dimension data</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Terminal</th><th>Typical dimensions</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>SAE post (positive / negative)</td><td>Top ~17.5 mm / ~15.9 mm, tapered</td></tr>
          <tr><td>JIS pencil post</td><td>~12.7 mm / ~11.1 mm, tapered</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Stud (marine / heavy duty)</td><td>3/8" threaded common</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="muted">
        Typical values — the taper and the positive-larger rule are the anti-reversal design; exact dimensions
        belong to the group's specification.
      </p>


      <h2>Why the exact fit matters</h2>
      <p>
        The battery must match the tray in length, width and height, and the terminals must match the cable ends and
        their <strong>position and polarity</strong>. A battery that is too tall can short on the hood; a terminal that is on
        the wrong side can prevent the cables from reaching. This is why "group size" is a fit spec first — the
        performance numbers (<a href="/">capacity and CCA</a>) come second.
      </p>

      <p class="muted">Return to <a href="https://data.worldbatteryhub.com">Battery Data</a> · <a href="https://worldbatteryhub.com">World Battery Hub</a>. Informational, not purchasing advice.</p>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
